$K = NumberWithUnits($C+273, 'degK');

#############################
# Exercise Group Introduction
#############################

BEGIN_PGML
To convert a temperature in degrees Celsius to degrees Kelvin, there is a formula [`K = C + 273\text{.}`]

END_PGML

######
# Body
######

BEGIN_PGML
What Kelvin temperature is [`[$C]^{\circ}C\text{?}`]

[@KeyboardInstructions('Use [|degK|]* for degrees Kelvin.')@]**

[_]{$K}{10}

END_PGML

